Kibana 8.19.23 for MidnightBSD

This distribution is licensed under Elastic License 2.0. Read LICENSE.txt
for its terms. This is a modified distribution, adapted by the MidnightBSD
ports project; these changes are not endorsed by Elastic.

MidnightBSD changes:
- Use the system Node.js 24 runtime, version 24.21.0 or newer. Prereleases
  and other Node.js major versions are rejected.
- Remove the bundled Linux Node.js, Chromium, and optional Linux scheduling
  addon. Upstream Piscina skips optional scheduling priority adjustment
  when that addon is unavailable.
- Disable reporting and screenshotting in the service launcher because the
  bundled Chromium cannot run on MidnightBSD.
- Keep configuration in /usr/local/etc/kibana and writable service data in
  /usr/local/www/kibana8/data. The service uses the upstream launcher so
  node.options and Node.js diagnostic options take effect.

Before upgrading from an earlier 8.x release:
1. Stop every Kibana instance. Mixed Kibana versions must not run together.
2. Back up configuration and take an Elasticsearch snapshot that includes
   the Kibana feature state before saved-object migration begins.
3. Upgrade Elasticsearch to 8.19.23 first, then upgrade Kibana. Preserve the
   existing Kibana data directory and its persistent instance UUID.
4. Review the new configuration samples and reinstall third-party plugins
   built for exactly Kibana 8.19.23.

See https://www.elastic.co/docs/deploy-manage/upgrade/deployment-or-cluster/kibana
